{"id": 20, "ts": 1780654660.2613244, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate the thoroughness of Sarah and James in outlining the strengths and gaps for Candidates\u202fC,\u202fB, and\u202fD. However, we still lack any concrete evidence of operational reliability or decision\u2011quality for Candidate\u202fA, and we have no data on his stress\u2011resilience, crew\u2011cooperation, or communication style. Given that reliability, calmness under pressure, and teamwork are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance flights, I cannot endorse a candidate whose core safety\u2011critical profile remains largely undocumented.\nBetween the two candidates with the most complete evidence\u2014C and B\u2014Candidate\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decisions, and positive crew atmosphere outweigh his communication difficulty, especially since we have no concrete examples showing that this difficulty has impaired cockpit coordination. Candidate\u202fB, while also stress\u2011resilient and conscientious, has a documented \u201cnasty remarks\u201d issue that directly threatens crew cooperation on extended routes.\nTherefore, I align with Sarah\u2019s provisional recommendation: **Candidate\u202fC** remains the strongest overall fit, pending the usual onboarding and development plan to address his communication and education gaps."}
